  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 209 AM MDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nThe heat is the main weather impact this weekend with a HEAT \nADVISORY continuing for the eastern Magic Valley, South Hills, and \nSnake River Plain. It's within these areas that highs today will \npush towards 100 degrees again and only drop into the low to mid 60s \novernight into Sunday. Some wildfire smoke lingers across the area \ntoday, but the main impacts from that are expected to be a bit more \nconfined to Custer County where an Air Quality Alert remains in \neffect through Monday afternoon. In addition to the heat and smoke, \na RED FLAG WARNING is also in effect for the Central Mountains this \nafternoon. This is due to gusty afternoon winds around 25 mph and \nminimum relative humidity falling to 10 to 15 percent. Outside of \nthis area, wind gusts will range from 20 to 30 mph with the \nstrongest gusts out across parts of the Arco Desert. There is a very \nsmall chance (10 to 15 percent) for an isolated shower or storm in \nparts of the South Hills and up north along the Idaho/Montana divide \nas a bit of moisture does its best to work up and around the high \npressure over our area. Expect Sunday to be a nearly identical \nweather day. The ridge of high pressure gets flattened a bit early \nnext week as an area of low pressure moves into British Columbia and \ntroughing extends southward into the Pacific Northwest. Where that \nlow will track throughout the rest of the week is not exactly \nresolved yet by the longer range models, but afternoon highs will \nslowly decrease during the week, falling to the low to mid 80s by \nnext Friday. Isolated shower and storm chances will be around \nthrough next week, but it may not be until the end of the week/next \nweekend that we finally see some potential for more widespread \nprecipitation.",
